		("PTCL-905", "OpenTPW draws the quads in the original's order (slots ascending, newest particle first, world and screen-space particles together) as runs of one blend ([EXT:particle-blend-runs]); the original submits one batch per particle (0x565F90 -> 0x565240) with its own state word, which the decoder 0x567620 turns into: 0x1256 opaque (no blend, no alpha test), 0x556 alpha blend with an alpha test at 0x10/255, 0x200522 one-plus-one and 0x200552 source-alpha-over-one with that alpha test, 0x2756 alpha blend with an alpha test at 0xF0/255, all with depth writes unless flags 0x4000 add 0x800; an untextured particle is opaque (0x1256) when its alpha byte is 0 or >= 0xF0, else 0x556 (0x57C6FA-0x57C71B), and flags bit 4 (0x200522, +0x30 for 0x2000) and 0x20000 (MAGFILTER point) modify it; a batch whose state lacks 0x1000 and 0x2000 (the renderer mask 0x3000, 0x5667D0) has its triangles depth-sorted within it (0x565590 -> 0x565490, only in renderer mode DAT_008BD524 = 1, or 4 without 0x1000), but a batch is one particle's two coplanar triangles, so the sort has no visible effect and is not a difference; the state words and their alpha tests and depth writes are not reproduced. Also a gap in the order against the world: a particle batch whose state has neither 0x1000 nor 0x2000 (0x556, 0x200552: the alpha and additive particles, and the weather's streaks and flakes) is kept by 0x565590 and drawn by 0x582AD0 in the same far-to-near list as the translucent world faces (sorted on the mean vertex depth, 0x5829E0), so a particle that lies behind water or a glass roof is seen through it; OpenTPW draws all particle, weather, pool-water and pool-spray entities after the whole sorted world list (Level.SplitLate, WorldPass), so a particle in front of water is drawn over it as before but one behind it is hidden by the water's depth. Porting the merge means turning every particle quad and weather streak into a sortable record, drawn individually in the middle of the world list, in place of the runs that share one dynamic vertex buffer and the draw order the particle tests pin.", "An alpha test in the particle shader (and its precompiled browser JSON), depth-writing and opaque material variants, and every particle quad and weather streak as a sortable record that joins the world's far-to-near translucent list"),
