ids 0x414420 loads from the type's archive: every *.emt member (pattern 0x788F40) at +0x4DC + 4 x atoi(the last character of its stem), so a template numbered 5 also takes the type's own sound list at +0x4F0, which type-10 sounds then submit as a category handle (ObjectTypeSounds plays nothing there); no shipped script names one literally, Jungle's porkpie EVENT takes its effect from a variable, and no shipped archive has a template numbered 5), the scoped message after the build effect (0x51C640; the upgrade's 0x51BFC0 is its sound, wired), the beam when a guest is created (0x4faec0, taken when 0x4fa990 finds none of five cell types), the staff members' beams (0x505790, 0x500bd0) and the online avatars (0x4f7c60), the first-draw beam 15 of the other vehicles (0x549DB0 sets flag 0x4000000 for every vehicle it creates, 0x54a009; its only reader is 0x546a89 in the per-vehicle draw 0x546280, which 0x519060 calls for every type-3 object with a controller, and no family check was found; OpenTPW raises it for karts only), the lobby's key-panel effect 0x61 (0x4b8ee0, 0x4b90f0, 0x4b9340; OpenTPW has no island lobby key panel, ADVISOR-025), the UI pool groups (0x5ED5A0 and its callers) and the message-tag UI particles 90 on first visibility and retained 91 at lifetime minus 5000 UI milliseconds (0x48de1a keeps 0x5b in control property 9; 0x48dfbe -> 0x486b90 requests 0x5a at the control centre); their timing is traced, but the HUD has no UI emitter ownership/rendering interface (docs/reverse/CHALLENGE-TERMINALS.md)", "What the variable of porkpie holds, the unset direction of the type-2 negative key, the cell types 0x4fa990 tests and the arrival cases that reach the guest beam, the staff, lobby and UI callers' triggers and operands, and whether a non-kart vehicle's first draw beams (a family check between 0x5467c8 and 0x546a89)"),
